<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
    <dict>
        <key>Description</key>
        <string>This download is NOT verified yet: Google publishes no hash for the file, and a check of the signature is not built, so nothing proves that the file is what Google published. The shared importer therefore refuses a real run of the cimian recipe unless the override sets pcman_allow_unverified to true. Downloads the current Google Drive for desktop installer for Windows (the EXE that Google serves at a fixed address), kept under the file name of the address, and then reads the version from the EXE itself with the shared processor WindowsExeVersion, because the address has no version in it. The address, the size and the date of the file were read by the writer on 2026-10-02, but this recipe was NOT rehearsed with AutoPkg: the first run on the build machine is the check of the rest. The recipe never stops on an unchanged download, so a failed import is tried again at the next run.</string>
        <key>Identifier</key>
        <string>com.github.serrc-techops.download.GoogleDrive-Win</string>
        <key>Input</key>
        <dict>
            <key>NAME</key>
            <string>GoogleDrive</string>
            <key>DOWNLOAD_URL</key>
            <string>https://dl.google.com/drive-file-stream/GoogleDriveSetup.exe</string>
        </dict>
        <key>MinimumVersion</key>
        <string>1.0.0</string>
        <key>Process</key>
        <array>
            <dict>
                <key>Processor</key>
                <string>URLDownloader</string>
                <key>Arguments</key>
                <dict>
                    <key>url</key>
                    <string>%DOWNLOAD_URL%</string>
                </dict>
            </dict>
            <dict>
                <key>Processor</key>
                <string>EndOfCheckPhase</string>
            </dict>
            <dict>
                <key>Processor</key>
                <string>com.github.serrc-techops.SharedProcessors/WindowsExeVersion</string>
                <key>Arguments</key>
                <dict>
                    <key>pathname</key>
                    <string>%pathname%</string>
                </dict>
            </dict>
        </array>
    </dict>
</plist>
